The address is the one `name` holds, an address or a DNS name, with the
netmask `netmask` holds.

It is plumbed on the device `dev` names, or on the one of the om network
`network` names, which also says the netmask and the gateway the
configuration does not set. A layer 2 network, as a l2_bridge one, says the
device only: the netmask is required, and no route is set but through the
`gateway` the configuration names.

Choose it for an address known in advance, as the one a DNS name of the
service resolves to.
